error[ffi_unknown_field]: `ffi-a-field-named-after-a-header-macro.h` defines `size` as a macro, and the type `BUF` binds has no member it names: C reads the macro's text where the field's name stands
  at tests/golden/unsupported/ffi-a-field-named-after-a-header-macro.hero:17:9
     |
  17 |         size: i32  #~ ffi_unknown_field
     |         ^^^^
  note: a group's `record` IS the header's type (§4.19), so a field is named exactly as the header names it: correct the spelling, or name the header whose `BUF` has a member `size`

